 "speech": {
  "language": "en",
  "text": "Why does acne happen? Well, there are a lot of possible reasons, but the root root cause is inflammation. So one big misconception, when I was growing up and I had really bad acne, at the time everyone talked about bacteria, acne causing bacteria. And so we would scrub our skin to try to get rid of the bacteria. It's even very common to be prescribed antibiotics when you have acne, it turns out that acne is actually caused by inflammation. And so if we want to get rid of acne, we need to find the source of inflammation. So it could be coming from nutrient deficiencies. It could be coming from inflammatory foods, gut issues, stress even. There's many different causes of inflammation. So it's a matter of figuring out for each individual person, what is causing inflammation for them.",
